118	Texas Bluebonnet	Lupinus texensis	Annual/Perennial	The Texas Bluebonnet is a flowering plant in the legume family, known for its striking blue flowers that bloom in spring. It is the state flower of Texas and features characteristic palmate leaves. The plant can grow in a variety of soil types and is often found in fields and along roadsides.	https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Bluebonnet-8100.jpg/960px-Bluebonnet-8100.jpg	Full sun to partial shade	Moderate, drought-tolerant once established	12 to 18 inches apart	1 to 2 feet tall	Spring	Easy	Plant Texas Bluebonnets in well-drained soil with full sun exposure. Water regularly, especially during dry spells, but do not overwater as they are drought-tolerant once established. Fertilization is usually not necessary, as they thrive in low-nutrient soils. Deadheading spent blooms can encourage further flowering.	t	f	f	f		native plant, wildflower, drought-tolerant, Texas	Fabaceae	Seeds or by transplanting seedlings		flower_garden	loam
9	Noble Fir	Abies procera	tree	The Noble Fir (Abies procera) is an amazing species in many ways. It is a tall and stately tree with a beautiful, conical shape; its symmetrical branches are heavily laden with needles that range from a deep, glossy green to a deep blue-green. It has a thick, scaly bark and splendid foliage that make it an ideal choice for any garden. Its wide, dense growth provides shelter to wildlife, while its strong branches provide it with excellent resistance to windstorms. The Noble Fir is a long-lasting species with impressive longevity, making it a great addition to any landscape. With its majestic form, lush color, and great strength, the Noble Fir is a remarkable species that will enhance any outdoor space.	https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/species_image/9_abies_procera/regular/49107504112_6bd7effb8b_b.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260309%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260309T063603Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=9a3c1b7c9c3c73dec463ba2cd95e2b1f8364c04b730274fbe5eb3d061aab5ba1	full sun	Average	Check manual guide	90-90 feet	Perennial	Medium	The Noble Fir (Abies procera) is an amazing species in many ways. It is a tall and stately tree with a beautiful, conical shape; its symmetrical branches are heavily laden with needles that range from a deep, glossy green to a deep blue-green. It has a thick, scaly bark and splendid foliage that make it an ideal choice for any garden. Its wide, dense growth provides shelter to wildlife, while its strong branches provide it with excellent resistance to windstorms. The Noble Fir is a long-lasting species with impressive longevity, making it a great addition to any landscape. With its majestic form, lush color, and great strength, the Noble Fir is a remarkable species that will enhance any outdoor space.	f	f	f	f	\N	\N	Pinaceae	Seed Propagation, Grafting Propagatio