105	Japanese Snowbell	Styrax japonicus	Deciduous tree or shrub	Japanese Snowbell is a small to medium-sized deciduous tree known for its stunning drooping clusters of white, bell-shaped flowers that bloom in late spring to early summer. It features dark green, ovate leaves that turn yellow in the fall, adding seasonal interest. The tree has a graceful, rounded habit, making it an attractive addition to gardens and landscapes.		Partial shade to full sun	Moderate, keep soil consistently moist but not waterlogged	6 to 10 feet apart	15 to 25 feet tall and wide	Spring to summer for blooming; fall for foliage color	Moderate	Japanese Snowbell prefers well-drained, acidic to neutral soil and can benefit from mulch to retain moisture and suppress weeds. Regular watering is essential, especially in dry spells. Pruning should be done after flowering to maintain shape and remove any dead or diseased branches. Fertilize in early spring with a balanced fertilizer to promote healthy growth.	t	f	f	f		ornamental tree, flowering tree, shade tree	Styracaceae	Can be propagated from seeds or softwood cuttings taken in late spring.		flower_garden	loam
29	Aoyagi Japanese Maple*	Acer palmatum 'Aoyagi'	tree	The Aoyagi Japanese Maple is a stunning sight to behold. It is a beautiful, compact deciduous shrub with highly textured, silver-green to yellow-green foliage that transforms to shades of maroon-red in autumn. Springtime brings clusters of small, rosy-red flowers that provide sweet nectar for butterflies and other pollinators. Aoyagi Japanese Maples make nice additions to rock gardens, small spaces, naturalized areas and even as specimen plants on larger properties. They grow best in part shade to full sun with well-drained, slightly acidic soil and average water. Highly ornamental, easy to care for and disease-resistant, the Aoyagi Japanese Maple is an amazing and rewarding choice for any landscape.	https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/species_image/31_acer_palmatum_aoyagi/regular/acer_palmatum_japanese_maples_trees_red_red_leaves_blue_sky_blue_white-1126158.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260309%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260309T063740Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=546ee6943bf420c740c88a9592ca4f727798254df1f2cb827c4a83aee49f0397	full sun, part shade	Frequent	Check manual guide	10-10 feet	Perennial	Moderate	The Aoyagi Japanese Maple is a stunning sight to behold. It is a beautiful, compact deciduous shrub with highly textured, silver-green to yellow-green foliage that transforms to shades of maroon-red in autumn. Springtime brings clusters of small, rosy-red flowers that provide sweet nectar for butterflies and other pollinators. Aoyagi Japanese Maples make nice additions to rock gardens, small spaces, naturalized areas and even as specimen plants on larger properties. They grow best in part shade to full sun with well-drained, slightly acidic soil and average water. Highly ornamental, easy to care for and disease-resistant, the Aoyagi Japanese Maple is an amazing an