30	Arakawa Cork Bark Japanese Maple	Acer palmatum 'Arakawa'	tree	Arakawa Cork Bark Japanese Maple (Acer palmatum 'Arakawa') is an amazing tree to include in any garden. With year-round interest, it has beautiful foliage and an unusual bark. The delicate, five-lobed leaves are bright green in summer, changing to orange and yellow in autumn. Its bark is striking with thick, corky ridges, giving an element of rugged beauty. Plus, it's great for small spaces since it only grows to 5m high and only takes around 10 years to reach its full size. Add it to a sunny but sheltered spot for the best performance.	https://s3.us-central-1.wasabisys.com/perenual/species_image/32_acer_palmatum_arakawa/regular/2560px-Montagnac-Acer-palmatum_04.jpg?X-Amz-Content-Sha256=UNSIGNED-PAYLOAD&X-Amz-Algorithm=AWS4-HMAC-SHA256&X-Amz-Credential=0MPGHU7CIPXNPMVWMXUW%2F20260309%2Fus-central-1%2Fs3%2Faws4_request&X-Amz-Date=20260309T063741Z&X-Amz-SignedHeaders=host&X-Amz-Expires=86400&X-Amz-Signature=33b93f968f71f68cfd681d79a22c213553d8931ff7327c7cc8fa8b718af8cf50	Full sun, part shade	Average	Check manual guide	15-15 feet	Perennial	\N	Arakawa Cork Bark Japanese Maple (Acer palmatum 'Arakawa') is an amazing tree to include in any garden. With year-round interest, it has beautiful foliage and an unusual bark. The delicate, five-lobed leaves are bright green in summer, changing to orange and yellow in autumn. Its bark is striking with thick, corky ridges, giving an element of rugged beauty. Plus, it's great for small spaces since it only grows to 5m high and only takes around 10 years to reach its full size. Add it to a sunny but sheltered spot for the best performance.	f	f	f	f	\N	\N	Sapindaceae	Grafting Propagation, Air Layering Propagation, Layering Propagation, Cutting, Root Division		flower_garden	loam
