108	Monkey Grass	Ophiopogon japonicus	Perennial ground cover	Monkey Grass, also known as Mondo Grass, is a hardy, evergreen perennial with arching, grass-like leaves that are typically dark green. It is often used as a ground cover, in borders, or as an accent plant in shaded areas. The plant produces small, white to lavender flowers in summer, which are less noticeable than its foliage.		Partial shade to full shade	Moderate; keep soil consistently moist but not soggy	12 to 18 inches apart	12 to 24 inches tall and wide	Year-round	Easy	Monkey Grass requires minimal maintenance. It should be watered regularly, especially during dry spells. Although it tolerates drought, it thrives in consistently moist soil. Pruning is not usually necessary, but old or dead leaves can be removed in early spring to encourage new growth. Fertilization is generally not required but a balanced fertilizer can be applied in spring for enhanced growth.	f	t	f	f		ground cover, shade plant, perennial, ornamental	Asparagaceae	Monkey Grass can be propagated by division in spring or fall, or by seed, although seed propagation is less common.		flower_garden	loam
